My first ascension - and damn it feels good!

Unfortunately I can't work out how to copy the picture and stuff from
the terminal window in XP (stupid Microsoft) so I'll have to give
edited highlights.

Gamma started with a magic marker and a spellbook of something boring,
like knock.  I blanked the spellbook in a fountain and wrote identify.
 I find that identify is extremely useful in the very early game.  In
the mines, I found not one but two magic markers.  I also found a helm
of brilliance.

Having three magic markers and the identify spell is Very Useful.

On the way to Sokoban I found speed boots in a shop.  Got the bag in
Sokoban.  The Quest was easy - perhaps too easy? - and the journey
down to Ludios was uneventful.  At Ludios I killed a silver dragon who
left scales - quickly made +5 SDSM using the markers.  Also picked up
a hawaiian shirt in Ludios which I enchanted to +4.

Medusa was easy - did it by tunnelling down and then coming back up
the stairs.

Got to the castle with a full AK (including 15 candles - 7 bought and
8 found!) apart from the gloves of dexterity.  Used a wish for those. 
Also used a wish for two scrolls of charging as I hadn't identified
them yet.  Used one on the wand of wishing and the other on a magic
marker.  Then recharged the other markers and enchanted the gloves up
to +5.

Left Castle with AC -40, around 300 HP due to alchemy and
reverse-genociding nurses in Sokoban, and around 370 SP.  Also had
port control from a Tengu and a ring of teleport.

Gehennom was boring.  The only interesting bit was Orcus, who summoned
lots of stuff.  I ended up having to fight Orcus, Demogorgon and
Yeenoghu in one huge battle.  Demogorgon is *very* hard.  Sorting
through the detritus from that one took ages...

Got to the bottom and nicked the Amulet.  Had a little difficulty with
Rodney on the way back up, but once I got shallow enough to be able to
teleport around levels it was cool.  No problems up to the Planes.

I entered the Astral Plane with a ring of conflict on (stupid!).  I
decided to have some fun because I had so many wishes spare (only used
two so far) so I got a pet Archon and a rubber chicken.  The rubber
chicken makes a big difference here!

And then ascended, eventually, after killing Famine 4 times, Death 3
times and Sickness 5 times.  I had a good wander around as I've only
been to the Astral Plane once before and I ended up ascending in
celestial disgrace.  Oops!

Lessons:
blanking a spellbook to get early identify spell is a good tactic
magic markers are great
reverse-genociding nurses in sokoban gets you lots of hp in the
mid-game
teleport control is extremely useful in gehennom
rubber chickens and magic missiles make the Astral Plane trivial

Interesting points:
never found a ring of slow digestion :-(
i've never seen this many candles in a game

Regrets:
i could have done this wishless
i should have done this wishless

Anyway, my next character is a Valkyrie - I'm ascending the classes in
reverse-alphabetical order as was suggested here a few months back. 
Wish me luck.  Oh, and I'll sort out how to copy from the window for
the next one ;-)

